Each cycle of the loop takes a ring around the outside of the grid, yielding its top row, then rightmost column, then bottom row in reverse, and then leftmost column in reverse. After removing each layer, the remaining rectangle is sent back to the top of the loop. Layers with only a single row or column are handled automatically, because the last three lines of the loop skip them entirely once the first line finishes. The loop does not stop until grid is empty.

