The function counts paths from the top-left to the bottom-right corner when each move is either right or down and the cells are blocked with 1s. When either the starting or ending cell is blocked, it returns 0.

It builds a table whose value at row i and column j is the number of valid paths from the start to that cell. The cell at (0, 0) is given 1 path, and each other unblocked cell gets the number of paths from above it plus the number from the left, so that the table builds up dependencies in one pass. The MDP is solved bottom-up on the grid, without path enumeration or memoization.

