and every cell must differ from its left and upper neighbour. Starting from the first two entries, the pattern determines what every cell should be. The next row must then also alternate, beginning with the opposite value of what the first row began with. A full row can be checked against a stored pair of expected values, swapped side to side on each row, and any deviation invalidates the grid. An empty grid or a single-cell grid is valid by definition, since there are no adjacent cells to disagree with.

