The two cycling steps can be understood as follows. The cycle of phases goes N/S, E/W, N/S, E/W forever. Each phase starts on the tick precedes a multiple of green_duration: the first N/S phase runs ticks 0 to green_duration - 1 inclusive, the first E/W runs green_duration to 2 * green_duration - 1, and so on. The phasestart and direction cycles are paired up the same way through zip, so each pair is a complete green phase, and a car arriving at tick t will be on the N/S phase at t = 0 and on the E/W phase at t = green_duration, with every other tick going the same phase as the one before it. A direction other than N or S correctly matches a phase only when that phase is the one carrying its letter, so only the E/W direction gets counted that way. A car in the E direction with t = 5 and green_duration = 5 reaches the end of one E/W green phase and falls into the next N/S phase and is rejected, which is why the intermediate assert returns 0.

