Each command modifies the document and the redo history. A 'do' appends its value and clears redo. An 'undo' removes the last value from the document and puts it on the top of redo, and a 'redo' pushes the top of redo back onto the document, all subject to the check that each operation only proceeds when there is a value to operate on. The final line returns the accumulated document.

